  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper reports that a Quantum LSTM (QLSTM) model achieves lower forecasting errors (RMSE 1.82, MAE 1.45, MSE 3.31) than classical LSTM (RMSE 4.79) and ARIMA (RMSE 6.52) on 10 years of Yahoo Finance data, and that a QSVM maintains higher adversarial robustness (accuracy drops of 11.67% under FGSM and 15.60% under PGD). It also compares reported QKD metrics (secure key rate 5.87 bps, entropy 0.99) with classical encryption schemes, claiming stronger long‑term security. However, the study does not report any concrete quantum circuit implementation, qubit counts, or hardware execution.",
